&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Partnership:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with Engineering and Product leaders to define roadmaps for foundational services that enable company-wide velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Foundations Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the planning and execution of programs in quality, reliability, compliance, and vendor/cost management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act as an Escalation Point:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide hands-on support for high-risk programs, helping the team navigate complex interdependencies and technical trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nurture Stakeholders:&lt;/strong&gt; Earn trust across the organization by managing expectations from leadership to individual contributors, ensuring accountability and clear communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimize Processes:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop &quot;light-touch&quot; frameworks for tracking OKRs and resource allocation that align with DoorDash’s fast-paced culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re excited about you because you have...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Depth:&lt;/strong&gt; You have a strong understanding of modern engineering practices, distributed systems, and cloud infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience in the Domain:&lt;/strong&gt; You have managed or driven programs specifically within data engineering, infrastructure, or developer platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; You have a track record of building consensus while dealing with the ambiguity of a rapidly evolving engineering landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execution Focus:&lt;/strong&gt; You operate at the lowest level of detail when necessary, reviewing technical specs and assessing trade-offs to ensure program success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empathetic Management:&lt;/strong&gt; You lead with empathy, seeking and providing timely feedback to foster an inclusive and innovative team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TPM Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 5+ years of experience as a TPM or Engineering leader, ideally within an infrastructure or platform organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Management Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; At least 2 years of experience directly managing a team of TPMs or engineers in a relevant technical domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Excellent written and verbal skills; able to convey complex infrastructure concepts to both technical experts and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong skills in project planning, estimating, and scheduling, with a focus on progress and pragmatic solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
