&lt;p&gt;The Global Safety and Security team advances DoorDash through the protection of people, property, operations, brand, and reputation. We manage safety and security risk and provide value across the business through technology, and a people-first approach. Our team strives to always be in front and there for our people anytime, anywhere.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Sr. Associate Project Manager, you will support the planning, execution, and delivery of projects related to physical security technology. You will collaborate with cross-functional teams to ensure projects are completed on time, within scope, and within budget. The role will require 25%+ travel. This role is ideal for someone looking to grow their career in project management within a fast-paced technology environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are excited about this opportunity because you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead project planning sessions, defining project scope, objectives, and deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate internal resources and third-party vendors for seamless project execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain detailed project schedules, tracking progress and making necessary adjustments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular project meetings, providing updates to stakeholders and addressing any issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with industry standards and best practices in physical security technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage project budgets and forecasts, ensuring financial accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the engineering, local business operation leaders, and accounting teams to align project goals with company objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare project documentation, including reports, meeting notes, and presentations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are excited about you because you bring…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Project Management, Engineering, or Business in a related field or an additional 4 years of work experience in quantitative or business fields&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of project management experience, preferably in the physical security technology industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of physical security technologies and best practices (e.g. Axis, Genetec, Mercury, Aiphone, Von Duprin, HID).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of physical security systems (e.g., video surveillance, electronic access control, electronic door hardware, intrusion detection, intercom).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, leadership, and interpersonal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in project management software (e.g., Smartsheets, Jira, Asana, Salesforce).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in budget management, cost management, and status reports.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in project management methodologies (e.g., Agile, Waterfall, Project Schedule Management via Ghhant Chart, Budget management, Cost Performance management).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security Platform Certifications are a plus. (e.g. Genetec, Axis, Software House, OpenPath)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PMP or equivalent project management certification is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 32px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
