&lt;p&gt;Sitting within the Brand Partnerships, Events &amp;amp; Hospitality team, this role is part of DoorDash&#39;s growing Global Events organization. Together, we shape how our brands come to life through experiences, partnerships, and hospitality, ensuring we show up consistently and meaningfully across every touchpoint.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a highly organized and execution-focused Senior Event Marketing Associate to support the growth of DoorDash Reservations and SevenRooms across North America. In this role, you&#39;ll help bring our brand to life through a mix of consumer-facing activations, restaurant partnerships, merchant events, industry conferences, and local market experiences. You&#39;ll work cross-functionally with teams to execute memorable experiences that drive awareness, engagement, and adoption of DoorDash Reservations. This is an ideal opportunity for someone who loves hospitality, thrives in fast-paced environments, and enjoys managing the details that turn great ideas into exceptional customer and merchant experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re excited about this opportunity because you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the planning and execution of North America event and experiential marketing programs for DoorDash Reservations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end event logistics for a variety of activations, including owned events, merchant pop ups, food festivals, trade shows, conferences, and partner activations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with restaurant partners, venues, agencies, vendors, and internal stakeholders to ensure successful event execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help develop and execute consumer-facing experiences that increase awareness, consideration, and engagement for DoorDash Reservations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage event production timelines, budgets, vendor contracts, shipping logistics, inventory, and on-site operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support sponsorship activations and strategic partnerships by coordinating deliverables, assets, guest experiences, and event programming.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Integrated Marketing, Social, Communications, Partnerships, Sales, and Customer Success teams to ensure alignment across campaigns and activations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track event performance metrics including attendance, lead generation, customer engagement, merchant participation, and overall program impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain event calendars, project plans, and reporting dashboards to support program visibility and operational excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to support on-site execution and serve as a brand ambassador at events across North America.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve processes, scale event operations, and enhance attendee experiences across the portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re excited about you because you have...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have&lt;strong&gt; 4+ years &lt;/strong&gt;of experience in event marketing, experiential marketing, field marketing, hospitality marketing, partnerships, or related functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have hands-on experience executing both consumer-facing and B2B events, with a passion for creating exceptional guest experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience interacting with AI tools (ie Claude, ChatGPT, etc) and display curiosity, adaptability, and the ability to blend AI with the day-to-day role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are highly organized and excel at managing multiple projects, deadlines, vendors, and stakeholders simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy rolling up your sleeves and can confidently manage event logistics from planning through on-site execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong project management skills and exceptional attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a proactive problem-solver who remains calm and resourceful in fast-paced environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience working with agencies, venues, vendors, and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are an effective communicator who can build relationships across teams and influence stakeholders through collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are passionate about restaurants, hospitality, dining experiences, and local communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable using data and reporting to evaluate performance and inform future event planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re willing to travel up to 25–35% across North America to support key activations and events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
