&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://click.appcast.io/greenhouse-te8/a31.png?ent=34&amp;amp;e=22630&amp;amp;t=1701374353806&quot; width=&quot;1px&quot;&gt; &lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://track.jobadx.com/v1/i.gif?utm_pixel=224e990b-8ff4-4287-8d5d-2ff09647f181&amp;amp;utm_ptz=EST&amp;amp;utm_rqt=track&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DoorDash, our mission is to grow and empower local economies. We believe that brand and creativity play a critical role in making that mission real for every customer, merchant, and dasher we serve. The Brand &amp;amp; Creative team plays a critical role in achieving that mission by earning an outsized share of people’s attention and engagement. We are not here to blend in, but to stand out:&amp;nbsp;to spark conversations, shape culture, earn attention and deepen connections.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a team of strategists, creatives, producers, marketers, and operators working together to turn business objectives into bold, effective, and emotionally resonant creative. We operate at the intersection of short-term impact and long-term brand building, ensuring every execution drives immediate results while strengthening how people feel about DoorDash over time. We believe that creativity is a business tool, and that when it&#39;s applied with focus, it drives not just awareness, but growth. This team owns the development, delivery, and evolution of the brand across every touchpoint, from major campaigns to always-on content.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brand &amp;amp; Creative Operations is the connective hub of the Brand &amp;amp; Creative org. Our team — Business Leads and Creative Operations — creates the conditions for great work: ensuring every project is strategically grounded, operationally sound, on-brand and creatively excellent. We’re embedded partners to Marketing, shaping how creative connects to marketing strategy, amplifies impact, and drives growth across the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Sr. Creative Project Manager (I5) is the operational driver who moves the creative work from brief to delivery –&amp;nbsp;connecting Creative, Production, Business Leads, Resourcing, Integrated Marketing and Channel teams with the clarity and momentum each project needs. You own the project plan, timeline, status and execution for a portfolio of projects. You bring strong PM discipline, production savvy, and a genuine appetite for improving how creative work gets done. This role manages a portfolio of 10-20 projects in a quarter spanning quick-turn content, paid social, digital and CRM campaigns, to large integrated campaigns, across all DoorDash audiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the Brand &amp;amp; Creative teams (including Creative, Social, Brand Partnerships) and Cross-functional Partners (including Integrated Marketing, Media) –&amp;nbsp;driving effective and efficient projects from start to finish.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own project intake end-to-end; build timelines, confirm resource assignments with the Creative Ops Lead and Business Lead, surface timing risks early, and hold the line on brief quality before any work kicks off.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage asset production and delivery, ensuring brand consistency and legal compliance, overseeing QA, and coordinating delivery to trafficking.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own project health reporting: maintain objective status in real time, lead weekly project reviews, and flag risks before they become delays.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execution &amp;amp; daily management: track progress daily, update timelines and resource allocations, communicate status proactively to stakeholders, and ensure production partners and creatives are aligned on timing and deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help manage third-party creative relationships, interfacing regularly with freelancers and production vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own project closeout: ensure all deliverables are transferred, documented, and stored correctly, with no loose ends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to capacity planning by surfacing project volume trends, flagging resourcing gaps, and keep project data clean and current in planning tools.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A pragmatic operator who knows how creative actually gets made –&amp;nbsp;across integrated campaigns, content, social, performance and retention channels – and who understands that the project manager’s job is to protect both speed and quality.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized and obsessively accountable – you treat timelines, budgets, and process hygiene as non-negotiable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator who can translate between creative teams, Business Leads, agency partners, and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive problem solver who anticipates risks, escalates early, and delivers calm under pressure.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable navigating ambiguity – able to make a call, move the work forward, and calibrate when to escalate versus solve it yourself.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care about the work – not just whether it shipped on time, but whether it’s good. You know when to push back on an unclear brief and when to protect the team’s process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5-7+ years &lt;/strong&gt;of project management experience in a creative agency or in-house brand/creative team. Experience managing integrated campaigns and familiarity with performance and retention channels is strongly preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience using project management tools (Monday.com, Airtable, Asana, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of managing complex, multi-deliverable projects, with multiple stakeholders and steering them to on-time delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with data-driven reporting and maintaining clear project health metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter mindset, with the ability to handle multiple projects with minimal oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with capacity planning or resourcing models; prior exposure to and practice with AI-enabled tooling for workflow efficiency.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
